        ":question/problem": "![](images/70/70b04ef6ee89c2bf06db99444f1f89afbe2ea15871f8f79da29668f7be3f9f97.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=2x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-1,-2)$, $B(1,4)$ and $C(2,4).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-1,-2)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x \\\\ (-2) & =2(-1)+0 \\\\ -2 & =-2\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x \\\\ (4) & =2(1)+0 \\\\ 4 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,4)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x \\\\ (4) & =2(2)+0 \\\\ 4 & =4\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line."
